{"qid":"Q23681","names":["Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus"],"title":"Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus","endonym":{"native":"Kuzey Kıbrıs Türk Cumhuriyeti","lang":"tr"},"capsule":"The Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus (Kuzey Kıbrıs Türk Cumhuriyeti) is a de facto state occupying approximately 3,355 km² in the northern third of Cyprus, created in the aftermath of Turkey's military intervention in July–August 1974, which followed a Greek military junta-backed coup aiming at enosis with Greece. Independence was unilaterally declared on 15 November 1983; UN Security Council Resolution 541 declared the act legally invalid, and only Turkey recognises the state. Some 30,000–40,000 Turkish troops are permanently deployed there. Successive rounds of UN-mediated negotiations, including the 2004 Annan Plan referendum, have not produced reunification.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The UN Buffer Zone (Green Line) established in 1974 and monitored by UNFICYP defines the territory's extent precisely; there is no ambiguity in the boundary.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Northern Cyprus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Cyprus"},{"label":"Britannica: Northern Cyprus","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Northern-Cyprus"},{"label":"UN Security Council Resolution 541 (1983), UN Digital Library","url":"https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/23479"}],"britannica":"place/Turkish-Republic-of-Northern-Cyprus","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Northern Cyprus","rulers":[{"qid":"Q200436","name":"Rauf Denktaş","start":1983,"end":2005,"image":"Rauf Denktash.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikime